From 7e01311ea1a84e7097e4d44432b30dbe00c2575d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:45:33 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 10/38] feat(engine): KVCR from a peer's HBM (kvcr.peer_hbm),
 off by default

web/sim.js kvcrPeerHbm: a KVCR pull may read a block the source rank's G2 lacks but its device KV
holds. With peer_hbm the registry tracks each rank's device-resident blocks from its device-tier
KV events (drained at pass end and after path B commands); a pull takes the source's G2 copies
(pinned until it lands, as before) and then its device copies (read as they stand, not pinned),
and counts the latter (KvcrStats::peer_hbm_blocks). Test: off, only the G2 prefix is pulled; on,
the whole prefix, with the device blocks unpinned; a device eviction is seen.
